&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Omada Health is seeking a Director to drive the day-to-day execution and operations of our GLP-1 solutions within our broader cardiometabolic platform. This leader will help translate Omada’s GLP-1 strategy into clear plans, workflows, and cross-functional routines that support rapid, high-quality scale. Working closely with the VP and key stakeholders, you will coordinate across product, clinical, data science, engineering, and commercial teams to ensure our GLP-1 program delivers measurable impact for members, customers, and Omada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will love this job if you enjoy turning complex strategies into structured execution, working in a fast-paced ever changing market, improving processes, enabling teams to perform at a high level, and driving accountable follow-through in a fast-moving, ambiguous environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team operations and ways of working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the VP to establish and maintain operating cadences, meeting structures, and communication norms for the GLP-1 program team and key cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and refine processes and tools that support collaboration, agility, and continuous improvement across product, clinical, data, engineering, and marketing partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help ensure GLP-1 program work is integrated with core Omada teams and workflows so that the program remains aligned with Omada’s broader cardiometabolic care model and member experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program execution and performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead day-to-day execution of GLP-1 program initiatives, converting strategy and ideas into clear project plans, timelines, and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on program OKRs and KPIs, including member outcomes, engagement, operational efficiency, and customer results, surfacing risks and opportunities early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage lightweight reporting and dashboards that provide visibility to Omada’s executive leaders and stakeholders, ensuring shared understanding of program performance and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and drive discrete improvement projects (e.g., workflow changes, automation opportunities, process updates) that support high-quality scale of GLP-1 and cardiometabolic care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate across clinical, commercial, product, engineering, operations, and regulatory partners to keep GLP-1 program work aligned, unblocked, and advancing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with sales, marketing, and customer success teams to support execution of GLP-1-related go-to-market and customer programs, including direct-to-employer and PBM channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain regular feedback loops with internal stakeholders and external customers to capture insights on member experience, operational performance, and market needs, and channel those into program iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market and program insight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a practical understanding of Omada’s GLP-1 programs, cardiometabolic care platform, and business model, including how GLP-1 care integrates with Omada’s virtual clinic for diabetes, hypertension, and related conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on GLP-1 and obesity care market trends across pharmaceutical manufacturers, digital health programs, and payer, PBM, and employer channels, and use these insights to inform execution priorities and stakeholder communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the VP and other leaders with concise input and perspectives that connect market signals to operational implications for Omada’s GLP-1 program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Values and leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model Omada’s values by cultivating trust, seeking context, acting boldly, delivering results, succeeding together, and keeping the mission at the center of daily work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a supportive, accountable environment for team members and partners, providing clear expectations and feedback and helping remove operational barriers to performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required experience and traits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 10–12+ years in digital health, health technology, or a related healthcare environment, with 3–5+ years leading complex program or operations work in high-growth or rapidly changing settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program and operational leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to run cross-functional programs, establish and maintain operating routines, and drive clarity and follow-through without needing to own overall company strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance and analytics orientation:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience defining and tracking program metrics, using data to identify issues and opportunities, and communicating insights to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to synthesize complex information and tailor messaging from frontline teams to executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product and market familiarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Understanding of digital health products, virtual care models, and cardiometabolic or chronic disease programs; experience with GLP-1s or obesity/chronic disease management is a plus but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfort operating in ambiguity and changing priorities, with a proactive, solutions-oriented approach to problem solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias for speed with judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to move quickly and make pragmatic decisions, while understanding the difference between irreversible, high-impact decisions and reversible, iterative choices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
